Item Value GoldenGate 19.1.0.0.4, classic Database Oracle 12.1.0.2 SE GG home /u02/Oracle/GG (host prd) Processes EXT1 (source GINESYS) → REP1 (target REPDB), unidirectional GG schema goldengate <p>Current <code>dirprm/ext1.prm</code>:</p> <pre><code>EXTRACT ext1
USERID goldengate@GINESYS, PASSWORD &lt;pwd&gt;
EXTTRAIL ./dirdat/aa
DDL INCLUDE MAPPED
TABLE RSBR.INVITEM;
</code></pre> <p><code>DDL INCLUDE MAPPED</code> replicates DDL for every mapped object, including <code>CREATE TRIGGER</code> on those tables. There is no lag history today, so lag incidents such as 29 Sep 2026 (13:20–13:45 IST) cannot be traced after the fact.</p>

Parameter Default Purpose <code>summarize_wal</code> off Run the WAL summarizer; required for incremental backups. <code>wal_summary_keep_time</code> 10d How long WAL summary files are kept. <code>sync_replication_slots</code> off On a standby: synchronise failover-enabled logical slots from the primary. <code>synchronized_standby_slots</code> ’’ On a primary: physical slots whose standbys must confirm WAL before logical consumers receive it. <code>transaction_timeout</code> 0 (off) Ends any transaction (idle or active) that runs longer than this. <code>allow_alter_system</code> on Set <code>off</code> to refuse <code>ALTER SYSTEM</code>. <code>event_triggers</code> on Set <code>off</code> to disable all event triggers temporarily (e.g. a broken login trigger). <code>io_combine_limit</code> 128kB Maximum size of combined reads for streaming I/O. <code>transaction_buffers</code>, <code>subtransaction_buffers</code>, <code>multixact_offset_buffers</code>, <code>multixact_member_buffers</code>, <code>notify_buffers</code>, <code>serializable_buffers</code>, <code>commit_timestamp_buffers</code> automatic / small fixed sizes SLRU cache sizes; raise for workloads with heavy subtransaction or multixact use. <code>enable_group_by_reordering</code> on Lets the planner reorder <code>GROUP BY</code> keys. <code>max_notify_queue_pages</code> 1048576 Maximum disk pages for the LISTEN/NOTIFY queue. <code>huge_pages_status</code> (read-only) Shows <code>on</code>/<code>off</code>/<code>unknown</code> for huge pages. <code>output_plugin_libraries</code> ‘pgoutput, test_decoding’ Added in 17.11. Allow-list of logical decoding output plugins (see below). <p>Example: stop runaway transactions for an application role</p> <pre><code>ALTER ROLE app_user SET transaction_timeout = '15min';
ALTER ROLE app_user SET idle_in_transaction_session_timeout = '5min';
</code></pre>

Node Role Host Database Primary Publisher 192.168.1.9 <code>learning</code> Standby1 Subscriber of primary, publisher for standby2 192.168.1.8 <code>learning</code> Standby2 Subscriber of standby1 192.168.1.7 <code>targetdb2</code> <p>Step 1. On standby1, set in <code>postgresql.conf</code>:</p> <pre><code>listen_addresses = '*'
wal_level = logical
port = 5432
</code></pre> <p>Step 2. On standby1, allow standby2 in <code>pg_hba.conf</code>:</p> <pre><code>host  all  logstd  192.168.1.7/32  scram-sha-256
</code></pre> <p>Step 3. Restart PostgreSQL on standby1:</p> <pre><code>pg_ctl restart -D /var/lib/pgsql/17/data
</code></pre> <p>Step 4. On standby1, create the replication user:</p> <pre><code>CREATE USER logstd SUPERUSER ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'abc';
</code></pre> <p>Step 5. On standby1, in database <code>learning</code>, create a publication with the table:</p> <pre><code>CREATE PUBLICATION mystd1 FOR TABLE reptab2;
</code></pre> <p>Step 6. On standby2, create the target database:</p> <pre><code>CREATE DATABASE targetdb2;
</code></pre> <p>Logical replication works between databases on different servers, even on different operating systems or architectures, and also between databases on the same server (see the same-cluster section above).</p> <p>Step 7. In <code>targetdb2</code>, create the structure of <code>reptab2</code>:</p> <pre><code>CREATE TABLE reptab2 (deptno int PRIMARY KEY, deptname varchar(20), city varchar(20), deptbuild varchar(20));
</code></pre> <p>Step 8. On standby2, subscribe to standby1’s publication:</p> <pre><code>CREATE SUBSCRIPTION mysub2
  CONNECTION 'host=192.168.1.8 dbname=learning user=logstd password=abc'
  PUBLICATION mystd1;
</code></pre> <p>Step 9. On standby1, check:</p> <pre><code>SELECT slot_name, active FROM pg_replication_slots;
\dRp
SELECT * FROM pg_stat_replication;
</code></pre> <p>Step 10. Insert a row on the primary and check that it reaches standby1 and standby2:</p> <pre><code>INSERT INTO reptab2 VALUES (3, 'IT', 'Montreal', 'ITBUILD');
SELECT * FROM reptab2;
</code></pre>

View Holds pg_database, pg_stat_database Databases and their activity pg_tables, pg_indexes, pg_views, pg_matviews, pg_sequences Objects pg_roles, pg_user, pg_authid Roles (pg_authid / pg_shadow hold password hashes; superuser only) pg_settings, pg_file_settings, pg_hba_file_rules Configuration pg_locks, pg_stat_activity Locks and sessions pg_stats, pg_statistic_ext Planner statistics pg_tablespace Tablespaces pg_available_extensions, pg_extension Extensions pg_timezone_names Time zones information_schema.* SQL-standard views of the same data <pre><code>SELECT current_database(), current_schema(), current_user, session_user, version();
SELECT current_setting('max_parallel_workers'), pg_backend_pid(), pg_postmaster_start_time();
SELECT inet_server_addr(), inet_server_port(), pg_is_in_recovery(), pg_is_in_backup();
SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_database_size('sales')), pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size('orders'));
SELECT pg_relation_filepath('orders');      -- file under base/
</code></pre> <p>Note: <code>pg_is_in_backup()</code> only reported old exclusive backups and was removed in v15.</p>
